(# Microsoft Fabric Learning Plan) Tj
T* () Tj
T* (## Purpose) Tj
T* () Tj
T* (This document is the master learning and implementation plan for building a Microsoft Fabric ) Tj
T* (platform from zero to production-ready maturity using an enterprise-minded, automation-first ) Tj
T* (approach.) Tj
T* () Tj
T* (## Delivery Principles) Tj
T* () Tj
T* (- CI/CD first) Tj
T* (- CLI second) Tj
T* (- Portal only as the last option) Tj
T* (- all non-secret platform artifacts belong in source control) Tj
T* (- prefer repeatable automation over one-time manual configuration) Tj
T* () Tj
T* (## Project Scenario) Tj
T* () Tj
T* (Northwind Unified Commerce is the reference platform used across the program. The business ) Tj
T* (needs a modern analytics platform for:) Tj
T* () Tj
T* (- batch sales, inventory, ERP, and supplier data) Tj
T* (- near-real-time e-commerce and store telemetry) Tj
T* (- governed semantic models and Power BI reporting) Tj
T* (- platform administration, security, governance, and day-2 operations) Tj
T* () Tj
T* (## Assumptions) Tj
T* () Tj
T* (- tenant region target is Canada Central unless a different region is required) Tj
T* (- learning begins on a Fabric trial and later transitions to paid capacity) Tj
T* (- Azure DevOps is the preferred Git and CI/CD platform for enterprise alignment) Tj
T* (- Microsoft Entra ID groups are used for access management) Tj
T* () Tj
T* (## Trial Constraints) Tj
T* () Tj
T* (- Fabric trial is time-limited and should be treated as a learning environment, not a ) Tj
T* (production endpoint) Tj
T* (- trial capacity does not represent the full enterprise networking posture) Tj
T* (- some advanced capabilities are limited or unavailable in trial) Tj
T* (- portal onboarding is still required for some initial activation tasks) Tj
T* () Tj
T* (## Target Architecture) Tj
T* () Tj
T* (### Logical Flow) Tj
T* () Tj
T* (1. Source systems land data into Fabric through pipelines, notebooks, and event ingestion.) Tj
T* (2. Raw data lands in OneLake bronze.) Tj
T* (3. Standardized transformations produce silver.) Tj
T* (4. Curated gold data supports analytics and serving layers.) Tj
T* (5. Lakehouse and Warehouse assets support data engineering and SQL-oriented access.) Tj
T* (6. Semantic models expose governed business metrics.) Tj
T* (7. Reports and dashboards serve business consumers.) Tj
ET
endstream
endobj
